This is a first pass implementation of a cover tree in c/c++.  It is
somewhat optimized and not terribly robust.  


'test_nn <int> <file>' checks the running times of tree creation and
			querying for <int> nearest neighbors for every point in <file>.

'knn <int> <file1> <file2>' computes the <int> nearest neighbors of every point in <file2>
			    amongst the points in <file1>

Copyright is owned by John Langford.

The code is licensed under the GPL.

The file 'cover_tree.{cc,h}' contains the core cover tree computation code. 
The file 'point.{cc,h}' contains the definition of a point as well as
parsing and printing functions.


Benchmark integration
---------------------
The original free functions and v_array layout are retained in namespace
original_cover_tree. Points are caller-owned const void* values. Construction
and queries accept a distance_function and optional context; use the same metric
for both. The callback returns the exact distance when it is <= upper_bound,
and may return any value > upper_bound otherwise. All distances/radii use double.
Query parameters are local to each call, allowing concurrent read-only queries
with thread-safe callbacks. Distance callbacks must not throw.

Results keep the original layout: each row starts with its query pointer,
followed by unsorted neighbor pointers; ties may return more than k neighbors.
The caller supplies IDs, sorting, and k clamping (1 <= k <= reference size).
Call free_tree(root) and free_results(results) to release their allocations;
these functions do not free the input points. v_array remains a shallow-copy
work array, so callers must not free copies of the same allocation twice.

The original batch algorithm and base=1.3 are preserved. Zero-radius groups use
exact zero distance; level work arrays grow as needed, and child counts use int.
The standalone examples keep the original numeric format, padding and loops.

CMake consumers can add_subdirectory this repository and link original_cover_tree.
Standalone build and correctness tests:
  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build -j
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
